  description: "A tall, curling stalk that opens into a wide, trumpet-like bell,
    with a second smaller bell weeping steadily from its underside into the soil
    below. \n\nIts bell holds far more than it looks like it should, feeding a slow,
    steady trickle into the soil around it long after the rain that filled it has
    passed."
  descriptionSecondary: ' A single placeable that plugs into up to 3 adjacent pots
    and keeps topping each one up toward a set water level automatically. Pllant
    it once among a cluster of thirsty pots and stop worrying about them.'
